Cross-Lingual NLU for Indian Languages
Project Overview
This project explores Natural Language Understanding (NLU) for Indian languages, focusing on intent classification, multilingual representations, and cross-lingual transfer learning.
The aim is to evaluate how effectively language models trained on high-resource languages can generalize to lower-resource Indian languages.
Objectives
- Build a preprocessing pipeline for Indian-language text.
- Establish a baseline for intent classification.
- Fine-tune pretrained IndicBERT models.
- Evaluate cross-lingual knowledge transfer across languages.
- Investigate the effect of transliteration and multilingual text normalization.
Tech Stack
Python, Google Colab, Hugging Face Transformers, Hugging Face Datasets, scikit-learn, PyTorch.
Weekly Roadmap
Week 1: Dataset exploration, preprocessing, and baseline intent classification.
Week 2: IndicBERT fine-tuning and hyperparameter experiments.
Week 3: Cross-lingual transfer learning and transliteration experiments.
Week 4: Evaluation, error analysis, and model demonstration.
Dataset
Amazon MASSIVE — multilingual intent classification dataset.
References
- AI4Bharat IndicBERT
- AI4Bharat IndicCorpV2
- AI4Bharat IndicNLP Transliteration
